# The build context must equal the tracked tree and nothing else. Everything
# below is gitignored data, agent/editor state, or a host-local cache: it
# either bloats the context past what Docker can tar in reasonable time, or
# imports a host artifact that can make an in-container check falsely green.
# exports/ is TRACKED — do not add it here.
#
# Verify after changing: the file list inside the image should match
# `git ls-files` exactly, in both directions. `tests/test_docker_context.py`
# holds the parts of that comparison a test can reach without a daemon.
.git/
.venv/
venv/
work/
# `**/` because a city's Overpass cache lives at configs/<city>/cache/, which a
# root-anchored rule misses: measured, 1.4 MB of warmed centerlines in the image.
# A warm cache there makes the fetch a cold start is supposed to make disappear.
**/cache/
deploy/
fixtures/
reference-src/

# agent and editor state — untracked, and the largest thing in the context
.claude/
.review-tmp/
todo.md
# machine-local notes, which live beside the document they annotate
**/*local.md

# host credentials; the image reads its keys from the run environment
.env

# the frontend linter's dev-only tree (make setup-js); nothing in the image
# runs it, and it is hundreds of megabytes on a box that has run that target
**/node_modules/

# Host-local caches: a stale one imported from the host is a false-green risk.
#
# `**/` is load-bearing on everything that nests. A .dockerignore pattern is
# ANCHORED AT THE CONTEXT ROOT — unlike the same line in .gitignore — so a bare
# `__pycache__/` excludes only the one at the top and every bytecode tree under
# src/, tests/ and scripts/ rides in. Measured, twice: both interpreters' .pyc
# files were in the image.
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.grimp_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info/
**/dist/
**/htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.coverage
.coverage.*
viewer/*/manifest.json
viewer/*/story-assets
viewer/*/og.jpg
viewer/cities.json
viewer/manifest.json
# The lab notebook. Untracked, and it would otherwise ride into the image as
# context: `experiments/*` with exceptions, for the same reason .gitignore
# spells it that way — the three named files are libraries the tests load.
planning_docs/
ROADMAP.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
scripts/experiments/*
!scripts/experiments/numeral_rules.py
!scripts/experiments/qualification.py
!scripts/experiments/water.py
